### Peak Empire -- Epic 2 manual test requests
### Run `pnpm functions:serve` first, then fire these one at a time.
### Base URL shown assumes the default emulator port/project layout --
### the real URL is printed in the emulator's terminal output on boot,
### copy it from there if it differs (format is usually
### http://127.0.0.1:5001/<project-id>/us-central1/<functionName>).

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:5001/demo-peak-empire/us-central1

### 1. Discover prospects via Google Places
POST {{baseUrl}}/discoverProspects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "industry": "dog walker",
  "city": "Calgary",
  "sources": ["google_places"]
}

### 2. Add a manual prospect (simulating an Instagram-only business)
POST {{baseUrl}}/addManualProspect
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessName": "Test Manual Prospect",
  "industry": "nail tech",
  "city": "Calgary",
  "instagram": "@testprospect"
}

### 3. Missing-field validation -- should return 400, not 500
POST {{baseUrl}}/addManualProspect
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessName": "Missing Industry Co"
}

### 4. Fetch the computed call queue
GET {{baseUrl}}/callQueue

### 5. Log a call against a real prospect id from step 4's response
POST {{baseUrl}}/logCall
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "prospectId": "PROS-REPLACE-ME",
  "outcome": "callback_requested",
  "summary": "Spoke with owner, busy season, call back after Nov 15",
  "followUpDate": "2026-11-15"
}
